  "Question": "A pool initially contains 100 m³ of water, and 4 m³ is drained each hour. The relationship between the volume of water $V$ (m³) and the draining time $t$ (h) is $V=100-4t$. The independent variable is:",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "$V$",
    "B": "100",
    "C": "4",
    "D": "$t$"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The volume of water $V$ changes as the draining time $t$ changes. Thus, $t$ is the independent variable and $V$ is the dependent variable.",
